      "title": {
        "en": "Compassionate care during difficult crises"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pet parents broadly commend the emergency clinical staff for showing genuine empathy and warmth in distressing moments. Reviewers praise gentle nurses, welcoming front-desk personnel who offer tea and comfort, and thorough attending doctors. Isolated reviews describe contentious conversations regarding prognosis and end-of-life options."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "communication",
      "sentiment": "mixed",
      "mentions": 7,
      "title": {
        "en": "Mixed experiences with clinical communication"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "While many clients report clear, step-by-step updates on their pet status throughout treatment, others cite significant communication lapses. Complaints include unreturned follow-up calls regarding unresolved symptoms, difficulty reaching night staff, and conflicting instructions between emergency triage and internal medicine departments."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "results",
      "sentiment": "mixed",
      "mentions": 4,
      "title": {
        "en": "Variable clinical outcomes in emergencies"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Reviewers note successful emergency stabilization for acute conditions such as accidental poisoning and eye ulcers. However, other clients recount situations where animals faced diagnostic uncertainties or complications that required transfer to specialized tertiary facilities for advanced interventions."
      }
    }
  ],
